-- title:
--   U_q = ± 1 on a ramified local component of H¹(Γ₀(L))
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a characteristic-zero complete discrete valuation domain with finite residue field $k = \mathrm{ResidueField}\,\mathcal O$, let $p \neq 2$ be a prime lying in the maximal ideal of $\mathcal O$, and let $\bar\rho$ be a residual Galois representation over $k$ (a two-dimensional $k$-space with an action of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q)$ trivial on some finite-level subgroup) which is absolutely irreducible, i.e. irreducible after base change to $\overline{k}$. Let $q \neq p$ be a prime at which $\bar\rho$ is not unramified: some valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ in its nonunits has an inertia element acting nontrivially. Let $L \neq 0$ with $q \mid L$, $q^2 \nmid L$, and let $S$ be a finite set of primes none of which divides $L$. On $H^1 = \mathrm{Hom}(\Gamma_0(L)^{\mathrm{add}}, \mathcal O)$ consider the operators $\mathrm{opFamily}$ attached to the generators $T_\ell$ ($\ell$ prime, $\ell \notin S$, $\ell \nmid L$), $U_r$ ($r$ prime, $r \mid L$) — both the transfer along $\mathrm{conjL}$ — and the diamond operators $\langle d\rangle$, $d \in (\mathbb Z/L)^\times$; assume they commute pairwise. Let $\bar\theta$ assign to each generator a value in $k$ such that for every prime $\ell \notin S$ with $\ell \nmid L$, every valuation subring $P$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $\ell$ and every $\sigma$ that is a Frobenius at $\ell$ for $P$, the characteristic polynomial of $\bar\rho(\sigma)$ is $X^2 - \bar\theta(T_\ell)X + \ell$. Assume moreover that $\bar\theta$ is realised on weight-two cusp forms: there is a ring homomorphism $\theta$ from the Hecke algebra $\mathbb T^S(L)$ (the $\mathbb Z$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathbb C}\,S_2(\Gamma_0(L))$ generated by the $T_\ell$, $\ell \notin S$, $\ell \nmid L$, and the $U_r$, $r \mid L$, $r \notin S$) to $k$ with $\theta(T_\ell) = \bar\theta(T_\ell)$ and $\theta(U_r) = \bar\theta(U_r)$. Let $\mathrm{Sp}$ be an idempotent splitting of the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra of $\mathrm{End}_{\mathcal O} H^1$ generated by the $\mathrm{opFamily}$ operators, that is, finitely many complete orthogonal idempotents $e_i$ together with maximal ideals $\mathfrak m_i$ exhausting all maximal ideals and satisfying $e_i \in \mathfrak m_j \iff i \neq j$; let $i_0$ be an index and $\pi_k$ an $\mathcal O$-algebra homomorphism from the corner ring $e_{i_0}\mathbb T e_{i_0}$ to $k$ with $\pi_k(e_{i_0}\,\mathrm{op}(g)\,e_{i_0}) = \bar\theta(g)$ on every generator $g$. Assume finally that every $v$ in the corner submodule $e_{i_0}\cdot H^1$ is parabolic, vanishing on all $\gamma$ with $\mathrm{tr}(\gamma)^2 = 4$. Then there exists $\varepsilon \in \mathcal O$ with $\varepsilon^2 = 1$ such that $\mathrm{heckeT}$ at $q$ acts on the corner submodule $e_{i_0}\cdot H^1$ by $v \mapsto \varepsilon\, v$.
--
--   This is the Atkin–Lehner type statement that at a prime $q$ exactly dividing the level, at which the residual representation is ramified, the operator $U_q$ acts as $\pm 1$ on the local component of $H^1(\Gamma_0(L),\mathcal O)$ cut out by the residual eigensystem; it is the form of the statement in which the eigensystem is additionally assumed to come from a homomorphism on the weight-two cusp-form Hecke algebra of level $L$. It feeds the construction of successive rungs in the level-changing ladder, being cited by [`CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_isCornerRealization_and_rung_of_isCornerRealization_of_dvd_of_not_sq_dvd_of_not_cube_dvd`](thm.html#CuspForm.heckeLocal.exists_isCornerRealization_and_rung_of_isCornerRealization_of_dvd_of_not_sq_dvd_of_not_cube_dvd).
